========================================================================================
READOUT
========================================================================================
1. The right scalar is excess e=p(k+1)-q.  Unit-excess rows create the large reciprocal depths; merely being below doubled-top is not enough.
2. In the exact grid k<=36,r<=12, the largest normalized depths are fixed r=4, r=3, and r=2.  No r>=5 row improves the depth constant.
3. On the k==1 mod30 branch, r=4 gives the known 4/(4k+3), but r=5,6,8,... quickly pick up excess 3,5,9,... and lose normalized depth.
4. The r=3 branch now has explicit residue-class witness formulas.  The next proof task is the matching upper cover certificate.
5. No o(1/k^2) dip was found in this continuation.
